4 "$(-\\infty ,-3)$ and $(3,\\infty )$" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534503 true] [17592186292244 1111 #uuid "36425b4d-aecc-59dd-afcd-476a5ecb7910" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292245 1034 "$(-\\infty ,-3)$ and $(0,\\infty )$" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534503 true] [17592186292245 1111 #uuid "cd287f3a-7a86-5f72-9d82-4c36657d016e" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292246 1034 "$(-\\infty ,-3)$ and $(-3,0)$ and $(3,\\infty )$" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534503 true] [17592186292246 1111 #uuid "183b364e-2f6e-5438-bde4-c1ddb2797290" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292247 1034 "(-\\infty ,-3)" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292247 1111 #uuid "095e3ea1-031c-54a8-bd35-01f7eab61423" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292248 1034 "$(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(3,\\infty )$" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534503 true] [17592186292248 1111 #uuid "5a08669b-29c3-5531-afbc-116e314974ee" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292249 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292250 13194139534503 true] [17592186292249 1089 "q-132666" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292249 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534503 true] [17592186292249 1100 "Find the values of $x$ for which the function $f(x)={e}^{2{x}^{2}-6x+3}$ is strictly decreasing." 13194139534503 true] [17592186292249 1113 #uuid "e994daf9-6dc5-55a7-aade-020d8278b5a2" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292249 1145 "The function is strictly decreasing where ${f}^{′}(x)<0.$ Differentiating $f(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)={e}^{2{x}^{2}-6x+3}(4x-6),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we need to solve the inequality\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2{x}^{2}-6x+3}(4x-6)<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe exponential function is always positive, so this reduces to\n\n$$\n4x-6<0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-6 & <0 \\\\ 4x & <6 \\\\ x & <\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the function is strictly decreasing on the interval $(-\\infty ,\\frac{3}{2}).$" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292251 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292252 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292253 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292254 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292255 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1041 "selection" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292253 13194139534503 true] [17592186292250 1110 #uuid "9e22d4c4-0ef8-5d39-bcc4-6bfcf42e6175" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292251 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,3)" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292251 1111 #uuid "8d4a439c-3760-59ae-a952-2d06efece4ba" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292252 1034 "x\\in (-3,\\infty )" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292252 1111 #uuid "912e14a8-a29a-50a7-a750-2601c5237d35" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292253 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{3}{2})" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292253 1111 #uuid "44fb95f6-be59-582b-abad-fcad5129bb73" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292254 1034 "x\\in (\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292254 1111 #uuid "45ab908e-f7fe-5596-9f80-61b384e27ab1" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292255 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292255 1111 #uuid "f57ab006-d7ec-56bd-b0c9-e86f260b841e" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292256 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292257 13194139534503 true] [17592186292256 1089 "q-132667" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292256 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534503 true] [17592186292256 1100 "Find the values of $x$ for which the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{2}+1)$ is strictly decreasing." 13194139534503 true] [17592186292256 1113 #uuid "0ca3eeff-b7f5-5d53-aae2-987010ec68f9" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292256 1145 "The function is strictly decreasing where ${f}^{′}(x)<0.$ Differentiating $f(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot 4x \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{2{x}^{2}+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we need to solve the inequality\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x}{2{x}^{2}+1}<0.\n$$\n\nThe function $2{x}^{2}+1$ is always positive. So, this reduces to\n\n$$\n4x<0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & <0 \\\\ x & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is strictly decreasing on the interval $(-\\infty ,0).$" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292258 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292259 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292260 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292261 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292262 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1041 "selection" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292262 13194139534503 true] [17592186292257 1110 #uuid "ec6af44c-714f-596f-a227-c145e9a51b58" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292258 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,1)" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292258 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292258 1111 #uuid "868bb96e-dd07-5c47-825c-10acbb5ebe98" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292259 1034 "x\\in (\\sqrt{2},\\infty )" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292259 1111 #uuid "12e3a044-d771-5cad-86ac-16428ca73b88" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292260 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\sqrt{2})" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292260 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292260 1111 #uuid "c110c872-9a41-53ea-b878-076c07c00a7e" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292261 1034 "x\\in (-\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{2})" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292261 1111 #uuid "1a25a8eb-1145-5fc1-bb38-4d7deea15be6" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292262 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534503 true] [17592186292262 1111 #uuid "a9d214a8-df34-524d-97ad-a0c59561f163" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292263 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292264 13194139534503 true] [17592186292263 1089 "q-132671" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292263 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534503 true] [17592186292263 1100 "Find the values of $x$ for which the function $f(x)=4{x}^{3}-27{x}^{2}-30x+9$ is strictly decreasing." 13194139534503 true] [17592186292263 1113 #uuid "4c459238-1e51-554b-a2be-46ee9a5e625e" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292263 1145 "The function is strictly decreasing where ${f}^{′}(x)<0.$ Differentiating $f(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =12{x}^{2}-54x-30 \\\\  & =6(2{x}^{2}-9x-5),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we need to solve the inequality\n\n$$\n6(2{x}^{2}-9x-5)<0.\n$$\n\nThe above inequality factors as\n\n$$\n6(2x+1)(x-5)<0,\n$$\n\nand the graph of $y=6(2x+1)(x-5)$ has roots at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=5,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014428/assets/7eec3fc84b851b3b39e5ae8ecff1343f39393d1dd8f7a6cce8e8904dc1c65d48.png)\n\nThe graph is negative on the interval $(-\\frac{1}{2},5)$ between the roots, so we conclude that ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ on the interval $(-\\frac{1}{2},5).$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is strictly decreasing on the interval $(-\\frac{1}{2},5).$" 13194139534503 true] [17592186292264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292265 13194139534503 true] [17592186292264 1000 #edb/ref 17